ic equations\n$x={t}^{3}+1,\\,y=3t$\nfrom $t=-2$ to $t=0$ (shown above)?" 13194139534461 true] [17592186289563 1113 #uuid "a5b96d4c-d45c-5b54-bef3-6984291ba3e9" 13194139534461 true] [17592186289563 1145 "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289565 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289566 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289567 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289568 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289569 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1041 "selection" 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289565 13194139534461 true] [17592186289564 1110 #uuid "734449f3-5639-5b38-93cb-6755b2c4403f" 13194139534461 true] [17592186289565 1034 "3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139534461 true] [17592186289565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534461 true] [17592186289565 1111 #uuid "23a35118-6509-5bc9-8ad